{
  "requirement": "{cite}`requirements.sdk.domain`\n\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain` reads an\n{term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain`'s nodes as values implementing\n`trust_but_verify::domain::NodeContents`. Reading includes the loading and preparation\nneeded to fingerprint and format the returned value; failures return the\ndomain's error:\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n\n    /// The application's representation of a node's contents.\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n\n    /// Load and prepare this node's contents.\n    fn node_content(&self, node: &Self::NodeId) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`.\n\n**Obligations derived from the text**\n1. `Domain::node_content` returns a value implementing `NodeContents` for a node.\n2. Reading includes the loading and preparation needed to fingerprint and format the value.\n3. A failure at any point, including preparation, returns the domain's error.\n\n**Success path**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[identities_remain_stable_and_fingerprinting_uses_the_supplied_snapshot]` reads through `read_snapshot`, which calls `node_content`. It asserts that `format()` returns \"before\". After the underlying data changes, it asserts that `fingerprint()` and `format()` still match the supplied snapshot. This shows the returned value carries what is needed for both operations.\n- `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[requirement_edges_and_input_freshness_use_the_sdk]` calls `HabeasDomain::node_content` directly. It asserts that the returned content's fingerprint equals the expected fingerprint, and that it changes after the source file changes.\n\n**Failure path**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[wildcard_versions_still_check_inputs_and_errors]` sets `fail_read`. It asserts that the domain's `Err(\"read\")` is returned unchanged through `is_current`.\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/validation.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` covers two failures. With `fail_read`, it asserts `ValidationError::Graph(\"read\")`. With `fail_prepare`, it asserts `Graph(\"render\")`. The `Memory` domain's `node_content` returns `Err(\"render\")` for `fail_prepare`, so this exercises a preparation failure. The test also asserts that no dependencies are recorded and that no agent call is made.\n\n**Conclusion**\nEach clause (value returned, fingerprint and format readiness, and the load and preparation failure modes) has a test with a relevant assertion. The test items carry {test} references to the subject.\n\nTwo obligations belong to refining requirements and are not assessed here: `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint` and `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.",
